 a head at a  housewarming party where someone decides  to burn across on the front lawn  to let letty and her housemates know how  they really feel  it's enough to get lady out there  showing how she really feels  she grabs a bat unleashes on the cars  parked out front  silencing the blowing horns that  neighbors have been using to terrorize  them since they first moved in  it's the first of two scenes where we  see letitia [ __ ] lewis and all her  glory  and i've gotta mention that journeys  millet really rises to the occasion here  it's a great scene and it is put  together really well  of course letty doesn't live in the  world where if someone comes to your  house  and burns a cross out front you'd be  forgiven for losing your temper when the  police arrive  they're not there to investigate the act  of terrorism but instead take her into  custody  and give her a rough ride with another  helping of intimidation  on top of clearly enjoying the power he  has over letty  the officer has some questions about the  house he asked her if anything weird has  been going on inside  and if someone told her to buy the  winthrop house in the first place  he can sense that she doesn't know what  he's talking about so he tells her that  the police found the parts of eight dead  black people in the basement  using the n-word to drive home the idea  that he won't lose any sleep if the same  thing  happened to the current occupants the  next day  she meets the ghost of the previous  homeowner face to face  or at least she inadvertently conjures  his face which tells her to get out of  his house  this leads her to investigate where she  learns that the head belongs to a fired  university professor named hiram epstein  he was the last person who lived there  he had a connection to the police  officer who was asking her questions  and this probably involved human test  subjects for the kind of experiments  that epstein got fired over ledy lays  out everything she's learned to tick 