ypes are trying to do  so i think it was a pretty good episode  i like the show's version of letty  even if i'm a little uncertain about  where things are headed  after she hooked up with tick the core  elements pertaining to who she  is are all there and the performance  really elevates things  i think it is a better episode than the  last one the pacing and transition still  seem a little off but i think they moved  from one story to the next in a way that  worked i wasn't a fan of the epstein  head coming up through the ground scene  but then really enjoyed the basketball  player with the baby's head  and the whole sequence where letty  managed to cast the spirits out it's  hard for me to look at it without  comparing it to the source material and  the expectations that go along with  having read it i was hoping they were  going to build the story out and go  deeper with things  but they decided to lean into the  monster of the weak format which is  probably what i liked  least about the book i'm still  interested to see where it goes from  here though  i will mention that they cut out a  pretty important part of the haunted  house story and that makes me believe  that they will probably circle back to  it  and that might mean that they're going  to blend the upcoming stories together  we only got a little bit of hippolyta  diana and montrose in this episode since  they didn't play a big part in what ledy  was going through at the house  i should mention that we saw hippolyta  find a model of the solar system which  definitely caught her interest  we also saw diana and her friends  playing with the ouija board  when they asked who they were speaking  to it spelled  george which might be her dad trying to  contact her but what it's spelled after  wasn't completely clear it's moving on  its own and it spells out the word dead  but there's also more letters that we  don't see on the screen  this stuff might have seemed a little  bit out of place but don't worry  you probably noticed by now that each  story sort of focuses on a particular  character  and just because they didn't play a big  part in this story doesn't mean they  aren't important and with that i'll  leave it there  let me know in the comments what you  thought about episode three  do you like the monster of the week  style or were you hoping for something  more akin to prestige tv  for lack of a better term did you like  the bat scene  or did you like letty bringing the  spirits together better  or if not one of those then what was  your favorite scene  please like the video if you enjoyed it  please subscribe to my channel if you  haven't already  thanks for watching i will talk to you  soon

